{"version":2,"text":"Vitamin C Deficiency: Texts\n\nText A\n\nScurvy is a life-threatening condition due to dietary vitamin C deficiency.\nThose affected are mostly refugees or victims of famine, alcoholics, older\npeople, fad dieters, or children with autism or idiosyncratic behavioural\nabnormalities. Diagnosis is often delayed due to incomplete review of dietary\nhistory.\n\nVitamin C deficiency may result from a diet deficient in fresh fruits and\nvegetables. Also, cooking can destroy some of the vitamin C in food.\n\nThe following conditions can significantly increase the body’s requirements for\nvitamin C and the risk of vitamin C deficiency:\n\nPregnancy\nBreastfeeding\nDisorders that cause a high fever or inflammation\nDiarrhoea that lasts a long time\nSurgery\nBurns\nSmoking, which increases the vitamin C requirement by 30%\n\nPage 406\n\nEmail: info@oetonline.net.au","layout":{"version":1,"width":595.276001,"height":841.890015,"blocks":[{"text":"Vitamin C Deficiency: Texts","lines":[{"text":"Vitamin C Deficiency: Texts","x":0.3232604685502852,"y":0.08192660652947642,"width":0.3360589955985812,"height":0.02569931893063252,"confidence":1,"words":[{"text":"Vitamin","x":0.3232604685502852,"width":0.09712472013465229,"confidence":1},{"text":"C","x":0.4267956604553255,"width":0.01753808314540132,"confidence":1},{"text":"Deficiency:","x":0.45074423888961723,"width":0.13909089877789316,"confidence":1},{"text":"Texts","x":0.5950059727000484,"width":0.06431349144881793,"confidence":1}]}]},{"text":"Text A","lines":[{"text":"Text A","x":0.058597695760289864,"y":0.15234305635517012,"width":0.06804268260765983,"height":0.022843839049451132,"confidence":1,"words":[{"text":"Text","x":0.058597695760289864,"width":0.04609859116426902,"confidence":1},{"text":"A","x":0.11034209826980747,"width":0.016298280098142225,"confidence":1}]}]},{"text":"Scurvy is a life-threatening condition due to dietary vitamin C deficiency.\nThose affected are mostly refugees or victims of famine, 